# SDET Capstone — Participant Preparation Guide

**Week 7 · Days 5 & 6 · Final Capstone**

This guide tells you **what to prepare** and **how the two days will run**. It is an
outline on purpose — the live site, the exact scenarios, and your individual
injected conditions are given to you on the day. Prepare the *skills*, not a script.

---

## 1. What the capstone is

You have spent seven weeks building automation skills in separate suites. In the
final two days you **assemble them into one integrated, production-grade quality
gate** that runs in CI against a **live, cloud-hosted travel-booking site** — and
you **prove it still holds when the site is deliberately broken underneath you.**

- **Day 5 — Build & integrate.** A full day of individual engineering. Goal by end
  of day: one integrated suite running green in CI, resilience built in, evidence
  assembled, and a demo dry-run completed.
- **Day 6 — Live gate.** You demo your suite live while real faults, a real
  performance regression, and a real DOM change are injected into the running
  site. Every diagnosis and explanation is **your own** — there is no AI in the loop
  and nothing is rehearsed on a happy path.

**This is individual work.** Everyone does the same engineering against a different
booking scenario and a different set of injected conditions.

---

## 2. What you will build

**One integrated suite, two projects, one repository, one pipeline** covering the
full stack:

| Layer | You automate | Concern |
|---|---|---|
| Web UI | the booking journeys | UI end-to-end, locators |
| REST API | the same journeys as an API | request/response contracts |
| Database | the data the API wrote | data-integrity / ownership assertions |
| Resilience | behaviour under injected faults | detect + diagnose + recover |
| Performance | a baseline + threshold | catch and explain a regression |
| Security | access-control + a scan gate | authorization negatives, scanner findings |

All of it wired together by a **single CI pipeline** that gates the merge and
publishes the evidence.

