## 4. Topics & skills that are covered (and graded)

Your work is scored across these dimensions. Prepare each one deliberately.

1. **Framework structure & quality** — both projects layered; thin tests; nothing
   hardcoded; locators and endpoints centralised. *(Reviewed first, weighted highest.)*
2. **Locator strategy** — semantic **role/label-first** locators; a **dynamic,
   relative, parameterised XPath** only where structure is the sole anchor. No
   absolute paths, positional indexes, or generated-class selectors.
3. **Integration completeness** — UI + API + DB against one live site, in one pipeline.
4. **Resilience under injected fault** — your suite **detects** the failure, you
   **diagnose the root cause**, and you show a circuit breaker opening and recovering.
5. **Performance** — a baseline, a threshold gate, and you **explain the anomaly** and
   verify it against a distributed trace.
6. **Security** — a scan gate plus **authorization / access-control negatives**.
7. **Secret test-data handling** — classify public vs secret data; resolve secrets at
   runtime; mask them everywhere; never in the repo, the reports, or the demo.
8. **CI pipeline** — two-job workflow, parallel tagged tests, security & performance
   gates, evidence as artifacts, merge blocked unless green.
9. **Locator resilience to a live DOM change** — when the page structure is changed on
   Day 6, well-built locators keep passing; any brittle one you diagnose and fix live.
10. **Coverage analysis + individual viva** — a traceability matrix by hand, and an
    honest judgement on where the risk is and what you would *not* automate.

